# Defence in depth. The Dockerfile copies an explicit allowlist and never uses
# `COPY . .`, so nothing below can reach an image even if this file is wrong.
#
# `.git` matters most: the historically exposed OpenAI key is still reachable in
# four commits of this repository's history, so the history must never be part
# of a build context that leaves this machine.
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes

# Secrets and local configuration.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.streamlit/

# The legacy Streamlit application: the only consumer of OPENAI_API_KEY.
ui/

# Local state, caches and build output.
.venv/
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.eslintcache
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Evidence. The client snapshot is copied in explicitly by path; everything
# else under .local is tens of gigabytes of full-scope corpora.
.local/evidence/candidates/
.local/evidence/releases/
.local/e2e-fixture-*/
.local/*.sqlite3

# Not needed at runtime.
tests/
docs/
*.log
*.md
